<!-- ll-accordion demo — mirrors the upstream docs page (#/components/accordion):
     intro, then the Examples entries with the page's own copy. Installation/
     Usage/API reference/Accessibility/Related are intentionally omitted.
     Note: the miniprogram panels open without the height animation (the
     reduced-motion behavior upstream) and the brace appears finished. -->
<view class="demo">
  <view class="demo-title">Accordion</view>
  <view class="sec-desc">Ruled rows that open. Each row sits on a hand-pulled pencil rule; a touched row gets a highlighter swipe, and an opened row turns its chevron over, writes a margin brace beside its text. Radix behavior is untouched.</view>

  <view class="sec">
    <view class="sec-h2">Examples</view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Questions</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">Ruled rows on a page. Opening one turns the chevron over, draws a margin brace beside the text (written top to bottom in blue pencil). `type="single" collapsible` opens one at a time and lets you close it again.</view>
    <view class="max-w-md">
      <ll-accordion type="single" collapsible default-value="item-1">
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-1">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Is it accessible?</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Yes. It follows the WAI-ARIA accordion pattern: one tab stop per row, arrows between rows, and every panel is labeled by its trigger.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-2">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Is it drawn by hand?</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Every rule, brace and highlighter swipe is a pen stroke, seeded so the same page always looks the same.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-3">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Does it respect reduced motion?</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Yes. With reduced motion the rows open at once and the brace simply appears.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
      </ll-accordion>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Several open, square bracket</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">`type="multiple"` keeps every row you open. `bracket="square"` swaps the brace for a square bracket, and `bracket={false}` leaves the margin empty. Buttons inside a panel keep their focus rings: an open panel is not clipped.</view>
    <view class="max-w-md">
      <ll-accordion type="multiple" bracket="square" default-value="{{['shipping', 'returns']}}">
        <ll-accordion-item value="shipping">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Shipping</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Orders leave the desk on Tuesdays and Fridays, wrapped in brown paper and tied with string.
            <view class="row"><ll-button variant="outline" size="sm">Track a parcel</ll-button></view>
          </ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="returns">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Returns</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Send it back within thirty days, unused and unlined.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="notes">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Gift notes</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>We write these by hand. Tell us what to say in the order comments.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="wholesale" disabled>
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Wholesale (closed for the season)</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>Back in spring.</ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
      </ll-accordion>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Account settings</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">A controlled accordion in a card: the open row lives in state, a button opens the next one, and the fields inside keep their rings and hover lines.</view>
    <view class="max-w-md">
      <ll-card>
        <ll-card-header>
          <ll-card-title>Settings</ll-card-title>
          <ll-card-description>Three short pages. Open them in any order.</ll-card-description>
        </ll-card-header>
        <ll-card-content>
          <ll-accordion type="single" collapsible value="{{settingsOpen}}" bind:change="onSettingsChange">
            <ll-accordion-item value="profile">
              <ll-accordion-trigger>Profile</ll-accordion-trigger>
              <ll-accordion-content>
                <view class="field">
                  <view class="field-label">Name</view>
                  <ll-input value="Ada Lovelace" aria-label="Name" />
                </view>
                <view class="field">
                  <view class="field-label">One line about you</view>
                  <ll-input placeholder="Mathematician, mostly" aria-label="One line about you" />
                </view>
              </ll-accordion-content>
            </ll-accordion-item>
            <ll-accordion-item value="notifications">
              <ll-accordion-trigger>Notifications</ll-accordion-trigger>
              <ll-accordion-content>We send a summary on Fridays and nothing else. Change that here whenever you like.</ll-accordion-content>
            </ll-accordion-item>
            <ll-accordion-item value="security">
              <ll-accordion-trigger>Security</ll-accordion-trigger>
              <ll-accordion-content>Passkeys are on. Two devices are signed in.</ll-accordion-content>
            </ll-accordion-item>
          </ll-accordion>
        </ll-card-content>
        <ll-card-footer>
          <view class="foot-note">Open: {{open || 'none'}}</view>
          <ll-button size="sm" bind:tap="nextStep">Next page</ll-button>
        </ll-card-footer>
      </ll-card>
    </view>

    <view class="sub-h3">Product details (long panels)</view>
    <view class="sec-desc">The shadcn demo: one row open at a time, the first open on arrival, and panels that hold more than one paragraph. Give AccordionContent a flex column and `text-balance` and the paragraphs space themselves.</view>
    <view class="max-w-md">
      <ll-accordion type="single" collapsible default-value="item-1">
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-1">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Product information</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>
            <view class="para">The Field Notebook is stitched by hand and lies flat on any desk. Its pages take fountain pen, felt tip and a careless highlighter without bleeding through.</view>
            <view class="para">Key features include a lay-flat spine, a ribbon that is always long enough, and an elastic that has never once snapped.</view>
          </ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-2">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Shipping details</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>
            <view class="para">We post worldwide with trusted couriers. Standard delivery takes 3-5 working days; express arrives in 1-2.</view>
            <view class="para">Every parcel is wrapped in brown paper and insured. You get a tracking link the moment it leaves the desk.</view>
          </ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
        <ll-accordion-item value="item-3">
          <ll-accordion-trigger>Return policy</ll-accordion-trigger>
          <ll-accordion-content>
            <view class="para">Send it back within 30 days if it is not right. If you are not completely happy, return it in its original condition.</view>
            <view class="para">Return postage is on us, and the refund is with you within 48 hours of the parcel arriving back.</view>
          </ll-accordion-content>
        </ll-accordion-item>
      </ll-accordion>
    </view>
  </view>
</view>
